  <h2>How to Choose the Right Loyalty Program</h2>
  <p>When reading our comparisons, we recommend judging programs based on your personal travel habits. There is no universally "perfect" points program, only the <strong>program that best fits your goals</strong>. Consider the following:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your Destinations</strong>: If you fly frequent short domestic hops, distance-based programs like Avios excel. If you want to fly to Europe in business class, Flying Blue might be easier to use.</li>
    <li><strong>Your Spending Habits</strong>: Do you spend heavily on dining and groceries, or is your spending mostly un-categorized? This determines which credit card ecosystem will earn you more points.</li>
    <li><strong>Your Tolerance for Hassle</strong>: Programs like LifeMiles require fewer miles for business class but suffer from poor IT and customer service. Determine if the savings are worth the potential headache.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Once you start redeeming, always run the math through our <a href="/en/calculators/points-vs-cash/">Points vs Cash Calculator</a> to ensure you are getting a good deal on every booking.</p>
</div>
